Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "UrbanFogDrivingScenario" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasObstacle :vehicle1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :foggyCondition1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Black sedan ahead in foggy conditions" .

:foggyCondition1 a :FoggyCondition .

:risk1 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility due to fog, leading to potential misidentification of obstacles or actors" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision risk due to obscured visibility of other vehicles, pedestrians, or road conditions" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Reduced visibility due to fog, leading to potential misidentification of obstacles or actors.
Severity Score: 0.85

**Risk 2:**
Description: Potential collision risk due to obscured visibility of other vehicles, pedestrians, or road conditions.
Severity Score: 0.75